{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>From the El of your father.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): from Him will come the will to help you, and from Shaddai, who overthrows the array of the stars, will come to you the blessing — ברכות שמים וברכות תהום — that you may be blessed in heaven and on earth. And likewise <b>blessings of breasts and womb</b> — that is, there shall reach you the blessings with which your father and your mother blessed you, as in the Targum. And know that the view of Onkelos concerning שדים is that it alludes to the father, because the male discharges seed like an arrow, from the Targum of שדי בימא (Shoot the arrow)." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: מאל אביך — your father is אביר יעקב, from Him will come to you the help after his reception of the influx from the heavens that he mentioned — and it is השמים, which receives from above; ועם שדי תהיה ברכתך — and it is התהום, which lies below; and they themselves are שדים ורחם, as in his Targum: ברכתא דאבוך ודאמך — the blessing of your father and your mother, in the manner of (Exodus 20:12) ״כבד את אביך ואת אמיך״ — by way of the secret, for the father and the mother correspond to them."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:44.334852135Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}